--   Test Description
--   
--   This test ensures that the GEM can handle collision retries when
--   the transmit buffers have various offsets.
--   
--   Functional Coverage
--   * Ensures that collision retries successfully recovers data from correct
--     buffer offsets.
--   
--   Detailed Test Description
--   
--   1. Setup wait states for the test.
--   2. Initialise the GEM for 100M mode operation.
--   3. Begin transmitting a three buffer frame which has an initial offset
--      for the first buffer in the frame.
--      Force a collision whilst the DMA is still reading the first buffer.
--      Verify that the frame is successfully retried using the correct offset.
--      Repeat the test three times with increasing offsets (1-3).
--   4. Begin transmitting a three buffer frame which has an initial offset
--      for the first buffer in the frame.
--      Force a collision whilst the DMA is still reading the second buffer.
--      Verify that the frame is successfully retried using the correct offset.
--   5. Begin transmitting a three buffer frame which has an initial offset
--      for the first buffer in the frame.
--      Force a collision whilst the DMA is still reading the third buffer.
--      Verify that the frame is successfully retried using the correct offset.
--   6. Begin transmitting a three buffer frame which has a zero offset
--      for the first buffer in the frame, but an offset for the second buffer.
--      Force a collision whilst the DMA is still reading the second buffer.
--      Verify that the frame is successfully retried using the correct offsets.
--   7. Begin transmitting a three buffer frame which has a zero offset
--      for the first buffer in the frame, but an offset for the second buffer.
--      Force a collision whilst the DMA is still reading the third buffer.
--      Verify that the frame is successfully retried using the correct offsets.
--   8. Check the statistics registers for correct values.
--
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------


-- ************************************************************************** --
--   1. Setup wait states for the test.
-- ************************************************************************** --
